+# Session 66 — push/rsp peephole soundness, VLA struct varargs; 4 more torture tests green
+
+Date: 2026-08-23
+
+Upstream base: `01a9eae2` (latest `ms178/lccc` main; PR #217 = session 65).
+Build: `cargo build --profile fastbuild --locked -j2` (Rust 1.98.0). The
+harness wiped the workspace mid-session; the environment was rebuilt from
+the merged upstream (fresh clone) with no work lost.
+
+## Delivered: 4 of the 6 remaining torture failures fixed
+
+### The peephole soundness bug behind 20040709-1/2/3 (cluster D)
+
+`eliminate_redundant_leaq` (local_patterns.rs) deletes a second
+`leaq X, %rax` when %rax "already holds" X. Its `written_families` helper
+handled `pop` (as writing the operand register — missing %rsp!) and did not
+handle `push` AT ALL: a push has no destination register operand, so the
+generic trailing-register fallback returned nothing.
+
+Both instructions MODIFY %rsp, and every cached `leaq X(%rsp), %rax` bakes
+the current %rsp into its address. After four pushes moved %rsp, a second,
+TEXTUALLY IDENTICAL `leaq 80(%rsp), %rax` computed a DIFFERENT address —
+and the dedup deleted it. sret calls passing a by-value struct hit exactly
+this coincidence (the 32-byte push adjustment made the sret-temp offset
+numerically equal to the struct argument's pre-push offset):
+`%rdi` received the struct argument's address, the callee wrote the return
+value into the argument, and the post-call memcpy restored garbage.
+
+Fix: `written_families` reports RSP as written for `push` (return early —
+no comma fallback), for `pop` (operand + RSP), and for `leave`/`enter`
+(rsp+rbp). All three bitfield tests pass at -O2.
+
+Regression: `tests/regression/push_rsp_leaq_dedup.c` (sret + by-value
+struct arg around pushes) at O0/O1/O2.
+
+### VLA struct varargs — 20020412-1 (cluster C)
+
+GCC's ABI passes a VLA-containing struct (runtime size) BY REFERENCE in
+variadic calls. Three coordinated changes:
+
+1. **Call sites** (both struct_arg_sizes paths — sig-based fallback and
+   pure inference): a VLA struct arg classifies as a plain pointer
+   (`dynamic_struct_value_size(a).is_some()` → None); struct lvalue
+   lowering already yields the alloca address.
+2. **Callee** (`lower_va_arg_struct`): a runtime-sized struct type fetches
+   a POINTER from the va_list (`VaArg` with Ptr result — the scalar GP
+   fetch checks gp_offset and reads the register save area) instead of a
+   zero-sized `VaArgStruct`; the surrounding assignment's runtime memcpy
+   copies the referenced data.
+3. **Runtime-size resolution** (`compute_vla_size_from_type_spec`): new
+   `Typeof(identifier)` arm — VLA locals now register their NAME in the
+   scoped `vla_typedef_sizes` table (previously typedef-only), so
+   `va_arg(ap, typeof(d))` reaches the size.
+
+Regression: `tests/regression/vla_struct_varargs.c` (two fetches — the
+va_list advance is exercised too) at O0/O1/O2.
+
