+
+## Remaining torture failures (2, fully designed)
+
+`20230630-2/4` — `__attribute__((scalar_storage_order("big-endian")))`
+bitfields. Design (verified against the test vectors):
+
+- Layout unchanged (bit positions identical); the STORAGE-UNIT ACCESS
+  transforms the bit window: for a field at unit-relative LSB-first bit
+  `p`, width `w`, in an `N`-byte storage unit, the reverse-SSO window is
+  `[N*8 - p - w, N*8 - p)` — i.e. bits are allocated MSB-first per byte in
+  memory order (equivalently: the unit value is byte-swapped).
+- Verified by hand for 20230630-2: `{341,1,1,1,1}` → unit 0x155F →
+  byte[0] = 0x15 = 21 ✓ (test expects 21).
+- Implementation surface: (1) parse the attribute in
+  `dispatch_gcc_attribute` (string arg via `parse_string_attr_arg`,
+  effective only when the order differs from `__BYTE_ORDER__`); (2) thread
+  the flag into `StructLayout` (needs a `TypeSpecifier::Struct` tuple
+  extension — 28 construction/match sites — or a parser side-table keyed
+  by tag; anonymous structs need the latter); (3) transform the bit window
+  in `resolve_bitfield_lvalue` (single-unit fields only; split-spanning
+  SSO fields need the split path extended).
+- NOT attempted this session: a rushed enum/plumbing change touching
+  every bitfield consumer risks the 461 green tests; the transform above
+  is the complete, verified design.
+
