+3. **SSO bitfields** per the design above.
+4. crc32 SIB fold (RA-01 follow-up) — GCC's remaining 13-instruction lead.
+5. ALU-source=load-dest relay peephole (`movl %eax,%r8d; addl %r8d,%esi`).
+
+## Do not
+
+- Do NOT dedup rsp-relative leaqs across push/pop boundaries (fixed, but
+  any new "identical instruction" peephole must model %rsp writes).
+- Do NOT classify VLA struct args by their compile-time size (0) — zero-
+  size classification silently drops the argument entirely.
+- Do NOT treat `typeof(d)` as unsized when `d` is a VLA local — the name
+  resolves through the scoped vla_typedef_sizes table.
